      "prompt": "What is printed when this positive-amount parser receives \"-10\"?\n\n```java\nint parseAmount(String text) {\n  int amount = Integer.parseInt(text);\n  if (amount <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Amount must be positive\");\n  return amount;\n}\ntry {\n  System.out.println(parseAmount(\"-10\"));\n} catch (IllegalArgumentException ex) {\n  System.out.println(ex.getMessage());\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "The program silently stores -10"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "Amount must be positive"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "-10"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "NumberFormatException"
        }
      ],
      "correct": [
        "b"
      ],
      "explanation": "-10 is syntactically a valid integer. The positive-amount rule rejects -10. The catch prints the message; no invalid expense is saved.",
